# The vendor reference library: datasheets, NXP's FRDM design-file package and
# Hiwonder's 186 MB chassis CAD. Every one of them was downloaded, not written
# here, and bom/README.md names, dates and grades each document - which is what
# makes it findable again. The .3dm is also past GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit.
# Present on disk, never pushed.
/vendor/

# Written by mechanical/make-assembly.py, which chdir's to its own directory,
# so both files have to sit beside it rather than under vendor/.
#   assembly.stl              pure output - delete it and re-run
#   chassis-3deck-fascia.obj  a SEED the script rewrites in place. It is not
#                             reproducible from the script alone; it started as
#                             a Rhino export of the .3dm. Back it up locally.
mechanical/assembly.stl
mechanical/chassis-3deck-fascia.obj

# fascia-lower.stl and fascia-upper.stl are tracked on purpose: OpenSCAD output
# shifts between versions, and these are the files that actually went to the
# printer.
